  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Given,</p><p>The line passing through the points&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi><mfenced><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Q</mi><mfenced><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>,</p><p>So, equation of line&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi><mi>Q</mi></math>&nbsp;will be,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mn>3</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mi>&#955;</mi></math></p><p>Now let point&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>R</mi></math>&nbsp;be&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mn>3</mn><mi>&#955;</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>4</mn><mi>&#955;</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>&#955;</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p>Given,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>R</mi></math>&nbsp;lies on plane&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>z</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8756;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>&#955;</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn><mi>&#955;</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>&#955;</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>&#955;</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8756;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>R</mi><mfenced><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p>Now let&nbsp;line&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>S</mi><mi>R</mi></math>&nbsp;be :<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>z</mi><mn>1</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mi>k</mi></math>&nbsp;as it is parallel to&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>7</mn></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mn>1</mn></mfrac></math>&nbsp;and passing through&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/e45b630c-53ea-4fcd-b4bf-b67d221457b6.png\" style=\"width: 250px; height: 175px;\" /></p><p>So, the point&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>S</mi><mo>:</mo><mfenced><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>k</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>k</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p>Now&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>S</mi></math>&nbsp;lies on plane :&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>z</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mfenced><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>k</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>+</mo><mfenced><mrow><mn>4</mn><mi>k</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>10</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mn>9</mn><mi>k</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>9</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></math></p><p>Hence,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>S</mi><mfenced><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#160;</mo></math></p><p>So, distance&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>S</mi><mi>R</mi><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mn>4</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></msqrt><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn></math></p>",
